# The build needs src/, the manifests and the tsconfigs. Everything else is either large,
# machine-specific, or — in `data/`'s case — the operator's, and belongs in the volume rather
# than baked into an image.
node_modules
dist
.git
.github

# Runtime data — all of it, with no exceptions to keep in step. What the image ships is
# `seed/`, which is not under `data/` and needs no carve-out here.
#
# It used to need one: `data/*` plus `!data/protocols/`, and when the knowledge base was added
# in 2026-08-28 nobody added `!data/kb/`, so `COPY data/kb/` found an empty context and failed
# the build. A `COPY` whose source depends on an exception in a second file is a release that
# breaks on a new directory.
data/

test
docker-compose.dev.yml
*.log
.DS_Store
